Reading: the MAP level tracks the largest level seen (logarithmic drift); the probability that the next
datum is unprovable by the posterior theory decays like 1/n; the regret grows like b*log n/log(1/rho)
when s = rho, and linearly when the theories' own level law s differs from rho (misspecification).
